## Behaviour and content

Write each language name in that language. Mark the current language programmatically, and use both `lang` and `hreflang` on alternative links. The full production document’s `lang` must match its principal content, while passages in another language need their own language attribute.

Only publish a translation after review by a suitably qualified speaker. Keep revisions in step and identify when an alternative version is unavailable or out of date. Do not silently substitute machine translation for a reviewed household instruction.

## Accessibility and testing

Check names and pronunciation with a screen reader. Test the actual equivalent destinations, page title, browser back, right-to-left layout where relevant, and long translated labels. Ensure a language change does not submit an unfinished control action.

## Home Assistant boundary and source

Keep native HA language preferences and translations. This reference does not change the account language or translate entity names. The [GOV.UK Language navigation component](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/language-navigation/) is currently in trial; record future changes before adopting them.
